 \"apply-is-pure\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/lib/import/stb/apply.ts imports only the Project type and local ST-Bridge types; no React, DOM, three.js, Next, zustand, or node:fs import was found. vitest.config.ts includes tests/**/*.test.ts in the domain project, and npx vitest run --project domain tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts passed 1 file / 15 tests.\",\n      \"note\": \"The source uses a unicode escape for the StbApplyResult type name; this does not create a runtime dependency.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no-framing-plan-coupling\",\n      \"verdict\": \"refuted\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A test-inclusive scan of src/lib/import/stb matched src/lib/import/stb/scope-guard.test.ts:53 ('applyFramingPlan') and :54 ('applyElevation').\",\n      \"note\": \"These are forbidden-name strings in the guard test rather than runtime coupling, but the premise explicitly requires tests to be included and the required scan is therefore not zero. Target code was not changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no-domain-drift\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"git diff main...HEAD --stat -- src/domain/ src/rulepack/ produced empty output.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no-rulepack-territory\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The required rule-term scan over every non-test .ts file in src/lib/import/stb produced NO_RULE_TERMS_NON_TEST_SOURCE. The source-only numeric review found only parser/application mechanics; scope-guard.test.ts still declares the complete forbidden term list.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"name-not-overwritten\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"apply.test.ts asserts result.project.name is unchanged and StbImport.test.tsx asserts the store project name is unchanged in the approval flows. The temporary project-name overwrite mutation broke 3 tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"refusal-preserves-project\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"apply.test.ts asserts changed-grid and changed-story refusals return applied:false and preserve the original project reference. Removing a refusal temporarily broke 2 tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"same-span-keeps-members\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"apply.test.ts contains the explicit 'keeps members when only labels change on an otherwise equal grid' case. Removing the same-span preservation branch temporarily broke that test.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"issues-survive-approval\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"StbImport.test.tsx passes the issue-bearing candidate through approval and asserts the issue remains visible. Temporarily clearing candidate.issues after approval broke 'keeps issues and unsupported elements visible after approval'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no-network-in-import\",\n      \"verdict\": \"refuted\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The required test-inclusive scan matched src/lib/import/stb/scope-guard.test.ts:49 ('fetch'), :50 ('XMLHttpRequest'), and :52 ('sendBeacon'). Runtime import sources contain no network call and telemetry contains no file-name or file-content payload handling.\",\n      \"note\": \"The matches are guard vocabulary strings, not runtime network calls, but the premise's stated scan includes tests and is not zero. Target code was not changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no-new-dependency\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"git diff main...HEAD --stat -- package.json package-lock.json produced empty output.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mismatch-issue-still-bites\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The mismatch issue is asserted by src/lib/import/stb/candidates.test.ts:268 and tests/fixtures/stb-import/expected/diffchecker-filea.json, and candidates.ts:127 adds it. Temporarily suppressing that line caused 2 failing tests: the UI candidate mismatch test and the diffchecker-filea candidate fixture test. The line was restored.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ledgers-not-fabricated\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The step-5 docs diff contains only docs/MILESTONES.md and docs/RISKS.md; ADR.md, PRD.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, and SOURCES.md are unchanged. Direct inventory found document=5, expected=5, applied=5, synthetic=2; STB_ISSUES=18 and STB_APPLY_REFUSALS=4; SOURCES.md records 4 real fixtures, RC real sample version 2.0.1, no realistic 2.1 corpus, and code-search total_count 9. These match the ledger values and the CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md ST-Bridge summary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"applied-fixtures-are-oracles\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"All 5 applied fixtures exist and each _derivedFrom points to the same-named expected fixture. Independent expected-to-applied derivation matched: diffchecker-filea X=1000,2000,2000,4400,4400,1000; Y=1000,3200,3200,3200,3200,3200,3200,1000; heights=4500,4000,4000,3800; dotnet X/Y=6000,6000 and 6000,6000; heights=5000,4200; hoaryfox X=3600횞6, Y=10800,3600, heights=4000횞5; mini X=6000,6000, Y=5000, heights=4000,3500; mini210 correctly has no applied grid/story values because both candidates are refused. The applied-fixture numeric mutation broke its fixture test.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"mutation_sweep\": [\n    {\n      \"mutation\": \"1. Swap applyStbGrid xSpans and ySpans.\",\n      \"broke\": [\"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > ST-Bridge candidate application fixtures > mini.json matches its independently derived applied fixture\", \"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > ST-Bridge candidate application fixtures > diffchecker-filea.json matches its independently derived applied fixture\", \"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > ST-Bridge candidate application fixtures > hoaryfox-sample.json matches its independently derived applied fixture\", \"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > applyStbGrid > keeps members when only labels change on an otherwise equal grid\", \"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > application result invariants > maps exactly one X and one Y grid without assuming their input order\"],\n      \"note\": \"Temporary mutation reverted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"mutation\": \"2. Reverse applyStbStories story IDs.\",\n      \"broke\": [\"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > ST-Bridge candidate application fixtures > mini.json matches its independently derived applied fixture\", \"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > ST-Bridge candidate application fixtures > dotnet-sample1.json matches its independently derived applied fixture\", \"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > ST-Bridge candidate application fixtures > diffchecker-filea.json matches its independently derived applied fixture\", \"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > ST-Bridge candidate application fixtures > hoaryfox-sample.json matches its independently derived applied fixture\", \"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > applyStbStories > applies the real candidate from bottom to top and leaves the grid unchanged\"],\n      \"note\": \"Temporary mutation reverted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"mutation\": \"3. Keep existing members instead of clearing them after successful story application.\",\n      \"broke\": [\"src/components/stb/StbImport.test.tsx > StbImport > does not change the project until story discard is explicitly confirmed\"],\n      \"note\": \"Temporary mutation reverted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"mutation\": \"4. Remove the changed-grid refusal while members exist.\",\n      \"broke\": [\"src/components/stb/StbImport.test.tsx > StbImport > does not change the project until grid discard is explicitly confirmed\", \"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > applyStbGrid > rejects a changed grid while members exist, preserving the original reference\"],\n      \"note\": \"Temporary mutation reverted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"mutation\": \"5. Remove same-span member preservation.\",\n      \"broke\": [\"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > applyStbGrid > keeps members when only labels change on an otherwise equal grid\"],\n      \"note\": \"Temporary mutation reverted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"mutation\": \"6. Overwrite project.name from candidate.projectName.\",\n      \"broke\": [\"src/components/stb/StbImport.test.tsx > StbImport > shows the candidate and independently applies its grid and stories\", \"src/components/stb/StbImport.test.tsx > StbImport > does not change the project until grid discard is explicitly confirmed\", \"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > applyStbGrid > discards members only when explicitly requested and preserves unrelated project data\"],\n      \"note\": \"Temporary mutation reverted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"mutation\": \"7. Clear candidate issues after successful approval.\",\n      \"broke\": [\"src/components/stb/StbImport.test.tsx > StbImport > keeps issues and unsupported elements visible after approval\"],\n      \"note\": \"Temporary mutation reverted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"mutation\": \"8. Add one to applied/mini.json xSpans.\",\n      \"broke\": [\"tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts > ST-Bridge candidate application fixtures > mini.json matches its independently derived applied fixture\"],\n      \"note\": \"Temporary fixture mutation reverted.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"test_counts\": {\n    \"files\": 97,\n    \"tests\": 1680,\n    \"delta_files\": 2,\n    \"delta_tests\": 21\n  },\n  \"diffstat\": \" AGENTS.md                                          |   1 +\\n CLAUDE.md                                          |   1 +\\n docs/MILESTONES.md                                 |   1 +\\n docs/RISKS.md                                      |   1 +\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/index.json                |  35 +-\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step0-codex.stderr.log    |   2 +\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step0-codex.stdout.log    | 119 +++++++\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step0-invoke.json         |   9 +\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step0-report.json         | 239 ++++++++++++++\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step1-codex.stderr.log    |   3 +\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step1-codex.stdout.log    | 132 ++++++++\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step1-invoke.json         |   9 +\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step2-codex.stderr.log    |   2 +\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step2-codex.stdout.log    | 155 +++++++++\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step2-invoke.json         |   9 +\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step3-codex.stderr.log    |  13 +\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step3-codex.stdout.log    |  95 ++++++\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step3-invoke.json         |   9 +\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step4-codex.stderr.log    |   2 +\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step4-codex.stdout.log    |  80 +++++\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step4-invoke.json         |   9 +\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step5-codex.stderr.log    |   3 +\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step5-codex.stdout.log    |  49 +++\\n phases/34-stbridge-apply/step5-invoke.json         |   9 +\\n src/app/page.tsx                                   |   2 +\\n src/components/stb/StbImport.module.css            | 127 +++++++\\n src/components/stb/StbImport.test.tsx              | 210 ++++++++++++\\n src/components/stb/StbImport.tsx                   | 364 +++++++++++++++++++++\\n src/lib/import/stb/apply.ts                        | 163 +++++++++\\n src/lib/import/stb/types.ts                        |  17 +\\n src/locales/ja.json                                |  29 +-\\n src/locales/ko.json                                |  29 +-\\n tests/e2e/uc23-stb-import.js                       | 164 ++++++++++\\n tests/fixtures/stb-import/applied/diffchecker-filea.json |  23 ++\\n tests/fixtures/stb-import/applied/diffchecker-mini210.json |  13 +\\n tests/fixtures/stb-import/applied/dotnet-sample1.json |  21 ++\\n tests/fixtures/stb-import/applied/hoaryfox-sample.json |  24 ++\\n tests/fixtures/stb-import/applied/mini.json        |  21 ++\\n tests/fixtures/stb-import/document/mini.json       | 122 +++++--\\n tests/fixtures/stb-import/expected/mini.json       |   4 +-\\n tests/fixtures/stb-import/synthetic/mini-sjis.stb  |   6 +-\\n tests/fixtures/stb-import/synthetic/mini-utf8.stb  |   6 +-\\n tests/stb-import/apply.test.ts                     | 335 +++++++++++++++++++\\n 43 files changed, 2622 insertions(+), 45 deletions(-)\",\n  \"unexpected_files\": [],\n  \"stb_importers\": [\"src/components/stb/StbImport.tsx\"],\n  \"noticed\": [\n    \"The exact coupling and network scans are refuted only because the test-inclusive scans see forbidden-term literals in scope-guard.test.ts; no runtime coupling or network call was found.\",\n    \"Step 5 added R16 to docs/RISKS.md, while the CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md summary tables still end at R15; this stale summary was not changed because docs were out of scope.\",\n    \"Final full test, lint, and typecheck passed. Lint has one pre-existing warning in src/app/api/oncall/alert/route.test.ts:161.\",\n    \"After reverting all mutations, target source is clean. The working tree remains non-clean only for the phase index/report being recorded and harness-created step6-codex.stdout.log and step6-codex.stderr.log, which are intentionally left uncommitted per AGENTS.md.\"\n  ]\n}\n\r\n===== src/lib/import/stb/scope-guard.test.ts =====\r\nimport { readFileSync, readdirSync } from 'node:fs'\r\nimport { join, resolve } from 'node:path'\r\n\r\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest'\r\n\r\nconst stbDirectory = resolve(process.cwd(), 'src/lib/import/stb')\r\n\r\nfunction nonTestTypeScriptFiles(directory: string): string[] {\n  return readdirSync(directory, { withFileTypes: true }).flatMap((entry) => {\r\n    const path = join(directory, entry.name)\r\n    if (entry.isDirectory()) return nonTestTypeScriptFiles(path)\r\n    if (!entry.name.endsWith('.ts') || entry.name.endsWith('.test.ts')) {\r\n      return []\r\n    }\r\n    return [path]\r\n  })\r\n}\n\nfunction decodeUnicodeEscapes(source: string): string {\n  return source.replace(\n    /\\\\u\\{([0-9a-fA-F]+)\\}|\\\\u([0-9a-fA-F]{4})/g,\n    (_match, codePoint: string | undefined, codeUnit: string | undefined) =>\n      String.fromCodePoint(parseInt(codePoint ?? codeUnit!, 16)),\n  )\n}\n\r\ndescribe('ST-Bridge document import scope', () => {\r\n  it('keeps the IR parser free of rule, section, network, and store concerns', () => {\r\n    const actualFiles = nonTestTypeScriptFiles(stbDirectory).sort()\r\n    const scannedFiles = actualFiles.map((file) => ({\r\n      file,\r\n      source: readFileSync(file, 'utf8'),\r\n    }))\r\n\r\n    expect(scannedFiles.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(3)\r\n    expect(scannedFiles.map(({ file }) => file).sort()).toEqual(actualFiles)\r\n\r\n    const forbidden = [\r\n      '若싩?',\r\n      '?띲겖泳숁뎸',\r\n      '?섉쎊',\r\n      '?뗣겤??,\r\n      'depth_cover',\r\n      'anchorage',\r\n      'cut_off',\r\n      'center_',\r\n      'StbSec',\r\n      'StbApply',\r\n      'StbColumn',\r\n      'StbGirder',\r\n      'StbBeam',\r\n      'StbWall',\r\n      'StbSlab',\r\n      'StbBrace',\r\n      'StbPile',\r\n      'StbFooting',\r\n      'fetch',\r\n      'XMLHttpRequest',\r\n      'WebSocket',\r\n      'sendBeacon',\r\n      'applyFramingPlan',\r\n      'applyElevation',\r\n      'updateProject',\r\n      'loadProject',\r\n      'useAppStore',\r\n      'zustand',\r\n      'createSampleProject',\r\n    ]\r\n\r\n    for (const { file, source } of scannedFiles) {\n      const sourceVariants = [\n        { label: 'original source', source },\n        {\n          label: 'unicode-decoded source',\n          source: decodeUnicodeEscapes(source),\n        },\n      ]\n\n      for (const { label, source: variant } of sourceVariants) {\n        for (const term of forbidden) {\n          expect(\n            variant,\n            `${file} (${label}) contains forbidden term ${term}; unicode escapes in identifiers can bypass this check, so the same check also runs on a decoded copy`,\n          ).not.toContain(term)\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  })\r\n})\r\n\r\n===== src/lib/import/stb/apply.ts =====\r\nimport type { Project } from '@/domain/model/project'\n\nimport type {\n  StbGridCandidate,\n  StbSkeletonCandidate,\n  StbSkeletonApplyResult,\n} from './types'\n\nfunction sameNumbers(left: number[], right: number[]): boolean {\n  return (\n    left.length === right.length &&\n    left.every((value, index) => value === right[index])\n  )\n}\n\nfunction sameStrings(\n  left: string[] | undefined,\n  right: string[] | undefined,\n): boolean {\n  if (left === undefined || right === undefined) return left === right\n\n  return (\n    left.length === right.length &&\n    left.every((value, index) => value === right[index])\n  )\n}\n\nfunction gridFor(\n  grids: StbGridCandidate[],\n  direction: StbGridCandidate['direction'],\n): StbGridCandidate | undefined {\n  const matching = grids.filter((grid) => grid.direction === direction)\n  return matching.length === 1 ? matching[0] : undefined\n}\n\nfunction gridValue(\n  xGrid: StbGridCandidate,\n  yGrid: StbGridCandidate,\n): Project['grid'] {\n  return {\n    xSpans: [...xGrid.spansMm],\n    ySpans: [...yGrid.spansMm],\n    xLabels: xGrid.axes.map(({ label }) => label),\n    yLabels: yGrid.axes.map(({ label }) => label),\n  }\n}\n\nfunction sameGridSpans(\n  project: Project,\n  nextGrid: Project['grid'],\n): boolean {\n  return (\n    sameNumbers(project.grid.xSpans, nextGrid.xSpans) &&\n    sameNumbers(project.grid.ySpans, nextGrid.ySpans)\n  )\n}\n\nfunction sameGrid(project: Project, nextGrid: Project['grid']): boolean {\n  return (\n    sameGridSpans(project, nextGrid) &&\n    sameStrings(project.grid.xLabels, nextGrid.xLabels) &&\n    sameStrings(project.grid.yLabels, nextGrid.yLabels)\n  )\n}\n\nfunction sameStories(\n  left: Project['stories'],\n  right: Project['stories'],\n): boolean {\n  return (\n    left.length === right.length &&\n    left.every(\n      (story, index) =>\n        story.id === right[index]?.id &&\n        story.name === right[index]?.name &&\n        story.height === right[index]?.height,\n    )\n  )\n}\n\nexport function applyStbGrid(\n  project: Project,\n  candidate: StbSkeletonCandidate,\n  options: { discardMembers?: boolean } = {},\n): StbSkeletonApplyResult {\n  const xGrid = gridFor(candidate.grids, 'X')\n  const yGrid = gridFor(candidate.grids, 'Y')\n  if (xGrid === undefined || yGrid === undefined) {\n    return {\n      project,\n      applied: false,\n      refusal: '?싥굤??숃짒?ゃ걮',\n    }\n  }\n\n  const nextGrid = gridValue(xGrid, yGrid)\n  const spansMatch = sameGridSpans(project, nextGrid)\n  if (sameGrid(project, nextGrid)) {\n    return { project, applied: false }\n  }\n\n  if (\n    !spansMatch &&\n    project.members.length > 0 &&\n    options.discardMembers !== true\n  ) {\n    return {\n      project,\n      applied: false,\n      refusal: '?ⓩ쓲?귙굤?싥굤??쉰?쎽툖??,\n    }\n  }\n\n  return {\n    project: {\n      ...project,\n      grid: nextGrid,\n      ...(spansMatch ? {} : { members: [] }),\n    },\n    applied: true,\n  }\n}\n\nexport function applyStbStories(\n  project: Project,\n  candidate: StbSkeletonCandidate,\n  options: { discardMembers?: boolean } = {},\n): StbSkeletonApplyResult {\n  if (candidate.stories.length === 0) {\n    return {\n      project,\n      applied: false,\n      refusal: '?롥숃짒?ゃ걮',\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (project.members.length > 0 && options.discardMembers !== true) {\n    return {\n      project,\n      applied: false,\n      refusal: '?ⓩ쓲?귙굤?롧쉰?쎽툖??,\n    }\n  }\n\n  const stories = candidate.stories.map((story, index) => ({\n    id: `story-${index + 1}`,\n    name: story.name,\n    height: story.heightMm,\n  }))\n\n  if (project.members.length === 0 && sameStories(project.stories, stories)) {\n    return { project, applied: false }\n  }\n\n  return {\n    project: {\n      ...project,\n      stories,\n      members: [],\n    },\n    applied: true,\n  }\n}\n\r\n===== src/lib/import/stb/types.ts =====\r\nimport type { Project } from '@/domain/model/project'\n\nexport type StbEncoding = 'utf-8' | 'shift_jis'\n\r\n// ST-Bridge 痍⑥엯 媛??④퀎媛 ?대뒗 ?ъ쑀 肄붾뱶????紐⑸줉?쇰줈留??쒗쁽?쒕떎.\r\nexport const STB_ISSUES = [\r\n  '野얍퓶鸚뽧깘?쇈궦?㎯꺍',\r\n  '?ゅ?恙쒌궓?녈궠?쇈깈?ｃ꺍??,\r\n  'XML鰲ｆ옄訝띹꺗',\r\n  'ST-Bridge壤℡폀?㎯겒??,\r\n  '?욅쎍雅ㅹ싥굤??,\r\n  '?ゅ?恙쒒싥굤??Ŧ??,\r\n  '?싥굤??궛?ャ꺖?쀦빊訝띴???,\r\n  '?싥굤??뼶?묇툖??,\r\n  '?싥굤??퇌??㎗?덁툖??,\r\n  '?싥굤??퐤營?뇥筽?,\r\n  '?싥굤??꺀?쇻꺂轝좄맼',\r\n  '?싥굤??쑋濾쒎눣',\r\n  '?싥굤??퐤營?겏影?밤겗訝띴???,\r\n  '?롢꺃?쇻꺂鰲ｉ뇠訝띹꺗',\r\n  '?롢꺃?쇻꺂?띹쨭',\r\n  '?겻툔?с깧?ユ쑋野얍퓶',\r\n  '野얍퓶鸚뽧겗?롧Ŧ??,\r\n  '?롣툖擁?,\r\n] as const\r\n\r\nexport type StbIssue = (typeof STB_ISSUES)[number]\r\n\r\nexport interface StbAxisRaw {\r\n  id?: string\r\n  name?: string\r\n  distance?: string\r\n  nodeIds: string[]\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport interface StbAxisGroupRaw {\r\n  groupName?: string\r\n  angle?: string\r\n  originX?: string\r\n  originY?: string\r\n  axes: StbAxisRaw[]\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport interface StbStoryRaw {\r\n  id?: string\r\n  name?: string\r\n  height?: string\r\n  kind?: string\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport interface StbNodeRaw {\r\n  id?: string\r\n  x?: string\r\n  y?: string\r\n  z?: string\r\n  kind?: string\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport interface StbDocument {\r\n  version: string\r\n  projectName?: string\r\n  encoding: StbEncoding\r\n  axisGroups: StbAxisGroupRaw[]\r\n  stories: StbStoryRaw[]\r\n  nodes: StbNodeRaw[]\r\n  unsupportedAxisKinds: { name: string; count: number }[]\r\n  unreadElements: { name: string; count: number }[]\r\n  issues: StbIssue[]\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport interface StbAxisCandidate {\r\n  label: string\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport interface StbGridCandidate {\r\n  direction: 'X' | 'Y'\r\n  groupName?: string\r\n  axes: StbAxisCandidate[]\r\n  spansMm: number[]\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport interface StbStoryCandidate {\r\n  name: string\r\n  heightMm: number\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport interface StbSkeletonCandidate {\n  version: string\n  projectName?: string\n  grids: StbGridCandidate[]\n  stories: StbStoryCandidate[]\n  unsupported: { name: string; count: number }[]\n  issues: StbIssue[]\n}\n\nexport const STB_SKELETON_APPLY_REFUSALS = [\n  '?싥굤??숃짒?ゃ걮',\n  '?롥숃짒?ゃ걮',\n  '?ⓩ쓲?귙굤?싥굤??쉰?쎽툖??,\n  '?ⓩ쓲?귙굤?롧쉰?쎽툖??,\n] as const\n\nexport type StbSkeletonApplyRefusal =\n  (typeof STB_SKELETON_APPLY_REFUSALS)[number]\n\nexport interface StbSkeletonApplyResult {\n  project: Project\n  applied: boolean\n  refusal?: StbSkeletonApplyRefusal\n}\n\r\n===== src/lib/import/stb/candidates.ts =====\r\nimport type {\r\n  StbAxisGroupRaw,\r\n  StbAxisRaw,\r\n  StbDocument,\r\n  StbGridCandidate,\r\n  StbIssue,\r\n  StbSkeletonCandidate,\r\n} from './types'\r\n\r\nconst AXIS_DIRECTIONS = ['X', 'Y'] as const\r\ntype AxisDirection = (typeof AXIS_DIRECTIONS)[number]\r\n\r\nconst SUPPORTED_STORY_KINDS = new Set(['GENERAL', 'ROOF', 'PENTHOUSE'])\r\n\r\nfunction addIssue(issues: StbIssue[], issue: StbIssue): void {\r\n  if (!issues.includes(issue)) issues.push(issue)\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction unsupportedItems(document: StbDocument): { name: string; count: number }[] {\r\n  return [...document.unsupportedAxisKinds, ...document.unreadElements]\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction normalizedAngle(angle: string | undefined):\r\n  | { direction: AxisDirection; radians: number }\r\n  | undefined {\r\n  const value = Number(angle)\r\n  if (!Number.isFinite(value)) return undefined\r\n\r\n  const normalized = ((value % 360) + 360) % 360\r\n  const quadrant = Math.round(normalized / 90)\r\n  if (Math.abs(normalized - quadrant * 90) > 0.001) return undefined\r\n\r\n  const quadrantInCycle = quadrant % 4\r\n  return {\r\n    direction:\r\n      quadrantInCycle === 0 || quadrantInCycle === 2 ? 'Y' : 'X',\r\n    radians: normalized,\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction originFor(group: StbAxisGroupRaw, direction: AxisDirection): number {\r\n  const rawOrigin = direction === 'X' ? group.originX : group.originY\r\n  return rawOrigin === undefined ? 0 : Number(rawOrigin)\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction hasNodeAtAxisCoordinate(\r\n  axis: StbAxisRaw,\r\n  direction: AxisDirection,\r\n  expectedCoordinate: number,\r\n  nodesById: Map<string, { x?: string; y?: string }>,\r\n): boolean {\r\n  return axis.nodeIds.some((nodeId) => {\r\n    const node = nodesById.get(nodeId)\r\n    if (node === undefined) return false\r\n\r\n    const coordinate = Number(direction === 'X' ? node.x : node.y)\r\n    return Number.isFinite(coordinate) &&\r\n      Math.abs(coordinate - expectedCoordinate) <= 1\r\n  })\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction gridForDirection(\r\n  group: StbAxisGroupRaw,\r\n  direction: AxisDirection,\r\n  document: StbDocument,\r\n  issues: StbIssue[],\r\n): StbGridCandidate | undefined {\r\n  const parsedAxes = group.axes.map((axis) => ({\r\n    axis,\r\n    distance: Number(axis.distance),\r\n  }))\r\n\r\n  if (parsedAxes.some(({ distance }) => !Number.isFinite(distance))) {\r\n    addIssue(issues, '?싥굤??퇌??㎗?덁툖??)\r\n    return undefined\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (\r\n    group.axes.some(\r\n      (axis) => axis.name === undefined || axis.name.length === 0,\r\n    )\r\n  ) {\r\n    addIssue(issues, '?싥굤??꺀?쇻꺂轝좄맼')\r\n    return undefined\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (parsedAxes.length < 2) {\r\n    addIssue(issues, '?싥굤??쑋濾쒎눣')\r\n    return undefined\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const sortedAxes = [...parsedAxes].sort(\r\n    (left, right) => left.distance - right.distance,\r\n  )\r\n  const hasDuplicate = sortedAxes.some(\r\n    (entry, index) => index > 0 && entry.distance === sortedAxes[index - 1]!.distance,\r\n  )\r\n  if (hasDuplicate) {\r\n    addIssue(issues, '?싥굤??퐤營?뇥筽?)\r\n    return undefined\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const spansMm = sortedAxes.slice(1).map(\r\n    (entry, index) => entry.distance - sortedAxes[index]!.distance,\r\n  )\r\n  if (spansMm.some((span) => span <= 0)) {\r\n    addIssue(issues, '?싥굤??퐤營?뇥筽?)\r\n    return undefined\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const nodesById = new Map(\r\n    document.nodes.flatMap((node) =>\r\n      node.id === undefined ? [] : [[node.id, node] as const],\r\n    ),\r\n  )\r\n  const origin = originFor(group, direction)\r\n  const hasMismatch = sortedAxes.some(({ axis, distance }) => {\r\n    if (axis.nodeIds.length === 0) return false\r\n    const expectedCoordinate = origin + distance\r\n    return !hasNodeAtAxisCoordinate(\r\n      axis,\r\n      direction,\r\n      expectedCoordinate,\r\n      nodesById,\r\n    )\r\n  })\r\n  if (hasMismatch) addIssue(issues, '?싥굤??퐤營?겏影?밤겗訝띴???)\n\r\n  const candidate: StbGridCandidate = {\r\n    direction,\r\n    axes: sortedAxes.map(({ axis }) => ({ label: axis.name! })),\r\n    spansMm,\r\n  }\r\n  if (group.groupName !== undefined) candidate.groupName = group.groupName\r\n  return candidate\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction gridsForDocument(\r\n  document: StbDocument,\r\n  issues: StbIssue[],\r\n): StbGridCandidate[] {\r\n  const hasArcOrRadial = document.unsupportedAxisKinds.some(\r\n    ({ name, count }) =>\r\n      count > 0 && (name === 'StbArcAxes' || name === 'StbRadialAxes'),\r\n  )\r\n  const hasDrawing = document.unsupportedAxisKinds.some(\r\n    ({ name, count }) => count > 0 && name === 'StbDrawingAxes',\r\n  )\r\n\r\n  if (hasArcOrRadial) addIssue(issues, '?욅쎍雅ㅹ싥굤??)\r\n  if (hasDrawing) addIssue(issues, '?ゅ?恙쒒싥굤??Ŧ??)\r\n  if (hasArcOrRadial) return []\r\n\r\n  if (document.axisGroups.length === 0) {\r\n    addIssue(issues, '?싥굤??쑋濾쒎눣')\r\n    return []\r\n  }\r\n  if (document.axisGroups.length !== 2) {\r\n    addIssue(issues, '?싥굤??궛?ャ꺖?쀦빊訝띴???)\r\n    return []\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const groupsWithDirections = document.axisGroups.map((group) => ({\r\n    group,\r\n    angle: normalizedAngle(group.angle),\r\n  }))\r\n  if (groupsWithDirections.some(({ angle }) => angle === undefined)) {\r\n    addIssue(issues, '?욅쎍雅ㅹ싥굤??)\r\n    return []\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const directions = groupsWithDirections.map(({ angle }) => angle!.direction)\r\n  if (directions[0] === directions[1]) {\r\n    addIssue(issues, '?싥굤??뼶?묇툖??)\r\n    return []\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const grids = groupsWithDirections.flatMap(({ group, angle }) =>\r\n    gridForDirection(group, angle!.direction, document, issues) ?? [],\r\n  )\r\n  return grids.sort(\r\n    (left, right) =>\r\n      AXIS_DIRECTIONS.indexOf(left.direction) -\r\n      AXIS_DIRECTIONS.indexOf(right.direction),\r\n  )\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction storiesForDocument(\r\n  document: StbDocument,\r\n  issues: StbIssue[],\r\n): StbSkeletonCandidate['stories'] {\r\n  if (document.stories.length === 0) {\r\n    addIssue(issues, '?롣툖擁?)\r\n    return []\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const levels = document.stories.map((story) => ({\r\n    story,\r\n    height: Number(story.height),\r\n  }))\r\n  if (levels.some(({ height }) => !Number.isFinite(height))) {\r\n    addIssue(issues, '?롢꺃?쇻꺂鰲ｉ뇠訝띹꺗')\r\n    return []\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  let hasBasement = false\r\n  let hasUnsupportedKind = false\r\n  for (const { story, height } of levels) {\r\n    if (story.kind === 'BASEMENT' || height < 0) hasBasement = true\r\n    if (\r\n      story.kind === undefined ||\r\n      (story.kind !== 'BASEMENT' && !SUPPORTED_STORY_KINDS.has(story.kind))\r\n    ) {\r\n      hasUnsupportedKind = true\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  if (hasBasement) addIssue(issues, '?겻툔?с깧?ユ쑋野얍퓶')\r\n  if (hasUnsupportedKind) addIssue(issues, '野얍퓶鸚뽧겗?롧Ŧ??)\r\n\r\n  const sortedLevels = [...levels].sort(\r\n    (left, right) => left.height - right.height,\r\n  )\r\n  const hasDuplicate = sortedLevels.some(\r\n    (entry, index) => index > 0 && entry.height === sortedLevels[index - 1]!.height,\r\n  )\r\n  if (hasDuplicate) addIssue(issues, '?롢꺃?쇻꺂?띹쨭')\r\n  if (sortedLevels.length < 2) addIssue(issues, '?롣툖擁?)\r\n  if (\r\n    document.stories.some(\r\n      (story) => story.name === undefined || story.name.length === 0,\r\n    )\r\n  ) {\r\n    addIssue(issues, '?롢꺃?쇻꺂鰲ｉ뇠訝띹꺗')\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (\r\n    hasBasement ||\r\n    hasUnsupportedKind ||\r\n    hasDuplicate ||\r\n    sortedLevels.length < 2 ||\r\n    document.stories.some(\r\n      (story) => story.name === undefined || story.name.length === 0,\r\n    )\r\n  ) {\r\n    return []\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  return sortedLevels.slice(0, -1).map((level, index) => ({\r\n    name: level.story.name!,\r\n    heightMm: sortedLevels[index + 1]!.height - level.height,\r\n  }))\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport function toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n  document: StbDocument,\r\n): StbSkeletonCandidate {\r\n  const issues: StbIssue[] = []\r\n  const unsupported = unsupportedItems(document)\r\n\r\n  if (document.issues.length > 0) {\r\n    const candidate: StbSkeletonCandidate = {\r\n      version: document.version,\r\n      grids: [],\r\n      stories: [],\r\n      unsupported,\r\n      issues: [],\r\n    }\r\n    if (document.projectName !== undefined) {\r\n      candidate.projectName = document.projectName\r\n    }\r\n    for (const issue of document.issues) addIssue(candidate.issues, issue)\r\n    return candidate\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const grids = gridsForDocument(document, issues)\r\n  const stories = storiesForDocument(document, issues)\r\n  const candidate: StbSkeletonCandidate = {\r\n    version: document.version,\r\n    grids,\r\n    stories,\r\n    unsupported,\r\n    issues,\r\n  }\r\n  if (document.projectName !== undefined) candidate.projectName = document.projectName\r\n  return candidate\r\n}\r\n\r\n===== src/lib/import/stb/candidates.test.ts =====\r\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest'\r\n\r\nimport type { StbDocument } from './types'\r\nimport { toSkeletonCandidate } from './candidates'\r\n\r\nfunction axis(\r\n  name: string | undefined,\r\n  distance: string | undefined,\r\n  nodeIds: string[] = [],\r\n) {\r\n  return { name, distance, nodeIds }\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction document(\r\n  overrides: Partial<StbDocument> = {},\r\n): StbDocument {\r\n  return {\r\n    version: '2.0.2',\r\n    encoding: 'utf-8',\r\n    axisGroups: [\r\n      {\r\n        groupName: 'X',\r\n        angle: '270.0',\r\n        axes: [axis('X1', '0'), axis('X2', '6000')],\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        groupName: 'Y',\r\n        angle: '0.0',\r\n        axes: [axis('Y1', '0'), axis('Y2', '5000')],\r\n      },\r\n    ],\r\n    stories: [\r\n      { name: '1FL', height: '0', kind: 'GENERAL' },\r\n      { name: 'RFL', height: '4000', kind: 'ROOF' },\r\n    ],\r\n    nodes: [],\r\n    unsupportedAxisKinds: [],\r\n    unreadElements: [],\r\n    issues: [],\r\n    ...overrides,\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\ndescribe('toSkeletonCandidate', () => {\r\n  it('maps directions from angles, never from group names', () => {\r\n    const candidate = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        axisGroups: [\r\n          {\r\n            groupName: 'X',\r\n            angle: '0.0',\r\n            axes: [axis('Y1', '0'), axis('Y2', '5000')],\r\n          },\r\n          {\r\n            groupName: 'Y',\r\n            angle: '270.0',\r\n            axes: [axis('X1', '0'), axis('X2', '6000')],\r\n          },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    expect(candidate.grids).toEqual([\r\n      { direction: 'X', groupName: 'Y', axes: [{ label: 'X1' }, { label: 'X2' }], spansMm: [6000] },\r\n      { direction: 'Y', groupName: 'X', axes: [{ label: 'Y1' }, { label: 'Y2' }], spansMm: [5000] },\r\n    ])\r\n\r\n    const unnamed = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        axisGroups: [\r\n          {\r\n            groupName: '?싥굤',\r\n            angle: '90.0',\r\n            axes: [axis('X1', '0'), axis('X2', '6000')],\r\n          },\r\n          {\r\n            groupName: 'other',\r\n            angle: '180.0',\r\n            axes: [axis('Y1', '0'), axis('Y2', '5000')],\r\n          },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(unnamed.grids.map((grid) => grid.direction)).toEqual(['X', 'Y'])\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  it('rejects the whole grid when either group is non-orthogonal and recovers when fixed', () => {\r\n    const nonOrthogonal = document({\r\n      axisGroups: [\r\n        {\r\n          groupName: 'X',\r\n          angle: '45.0',\r\n          axes: [axis('X1', '0'), axis('X2', '6000')],\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          groupName: 'Y',\r\n          angle: '0.0',\r\n          axes: [axis('Y1', '0'), axis('Y2', '5000')],\r\n        },\r\n      ],\r\n    })\r\n\r\n    expect(toSkeletonCandidate(nonOrthogonal).grids).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(toSkeletonCandidate(nonOrthogonal).issues).toEqual(['?욅쎍雅ㅹ싥굤??])\r\n\r\n    nonOrthogonal.axisGroups[0]!.angle = '270.0'\r\n    expect(toSkeletonCandidate(nonOrthogonal).grids).toHaveLength(2)\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  it('deduplicates issue codes when both axis groups fail the same rule', () => {\r\n    const bothNonOrthogonal = document({\r\n      axisGroups: [\r\n        { groupName: 'X', angle: '45.0', axes: [axis('X1', '0'), axis('X2', '6000')] },\r\n        { groupName: 'Y', angle: '135.0', axes: [axis('Y1', '0'), axis('Y2', '5000')] },\r\n      ],\r\n    })\r\n    expect(toSkeletonCandidate(bothNonOrthogonal).issues).toEqual(['?욅쎍雅ㅹ싥굤??])\r\n\r\n    const bothInvalidDistance = document({\r\n      axisGroups: [\r\n        { groupName: 'X', angle: '270.0', axes: [axis('X1', undefined), axis('X2', '6000')] },\r\n        { groupName: 'Y', angle: '0.0', axes: [axis('Y1', 'abc'), axis('Y2', '5000')] },\r\n      ],\r\n    })\r\n    expect(toSkeletonCandidate(bothInvalidDistance).issues).toEqual(['?싥굤??퇌??㎗?덁툖??])\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  it('rejects missing or non-pair axis groups without inventing a grid', () => {\r\n    const empty = toSkeletonCandidate(document({ axisGroups: [] }))\r\n    expect(empty.grids).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(empty.issues).toEqual(['?싥굤??쑋濾쒎눣'])\r\n\r\n    const one = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({ axisGroups: [document().axisGroups[0]!] }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(one.grids).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(one.issues).toEqual(['?싥굤??궛?ャ꺖?쀦빊訝띴???])\r\n\r\n    const three = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({ axisGroups: [...document().axisGroups, document().axisGroups[0]!] }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(three.grids).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(three.issues).toEqual(['?싥굤??궛?ャ꺖?쀦빊訝띴???])\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  it('accepts right angles within the documented tolerance', () => {\r\n    const candidate = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        axisGroups: [\r\n          { groupName: 'X', angle: '0.0', axes: [axis('Y1', '0'), axis('Y2', '5000')] },\r\n          { groupName: 'Y', angle: '89.9995', axes: [axis('X1', '0'), axis('X2', '6000')] },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(candidate.issues).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(candidate.grids.map((grid) => grid.direction)).toEqual(['X', 'Y'])\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  it('rejects parallel axes and arc/radial axes, but ignores drawing axes while continuing', () => {\r\n    const parallel = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        axisGroups: [\r\n          { groupName: 'one', angle: '0', axes: [axis('A1', '0'), axis('A2', '100')] },\r\n          { groupName: 'two', angle: '0', axes: [axis('B1', '0'), axis('B2', '200')] },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(parallel.grids).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(parallel.issues).toEqual(['?싥굤??뼶?묇툖??])\r\n\r\n    const arc = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        unsupportedAxisKinds: [{ name: 'StbArcAxes', count: 1 }],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(arc.grids).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(arc.issues).toEqual(['?욅쎍雅ㅹ싥굤??])\r\n\r\n    const drawing = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        unsupportedAxisKinds: [{ name: 'StbDrawingAxes', count: 1 }],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(drawing.grids).toHaveLength(2)\r\n    expect(drawing.issues).toEqual(['?ゅ?恙쒒싥굤??Ŧ??])\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  it('rejects invalid, missing, duplicate, and insufficient axis positions without inventing labels', () => {\r\n    const invalidDistance = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        axisGroups: [\r\n          { groupName: 'X', angle: '270', axes: [axis('X1', undefined), axis('X2', '6000')] },\r\n          { groupName: 'Y', angle: '0', axes: [axis('Y1', '0'), axis('Y2', '5000')] },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(invalidDistance.grids).toEqual([\r\n      { direction: 'Y', groupName: 'Y', axes: [{ label: 'Y1' }, { label: 'Y2' }], spansMm: [5000] },\r\n    ])\r\n    expect(invalidDistance.issues).toEqual(['?싥굤??퇌??㎗?덁툖??])\r\n\r\n    const missingLabel = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        axisGroups: [\r\n          { groupName: 'X', angle: '270', axes: [axis(undefined, '0'), axis('X2', '6000')] },\r\n          { groupName: 'Y', angle: '0', axes: [axis('Y1', '0'), axis('Y2', '5000')] },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(missingLabel.grids).toEqual([\r\n      { direction: 'Y', groupName: 'Y', axes: [{ label: 'Y1' }, { label: 'Y2' }], spansMm: [5000] },\r\n    ])\r\n    expect(missingLabel.issues).toEqual(['?싥굤??꺀?쇻꺂轝좄맼'])\r\n\r\n    const duplicate = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        axisGroups: [\r\n          { groupName: 'X', angle: '270', axes: [axis('X1', '0'), axis('X2', '0')] },\r\n          { groupName: 'Y', angle: '0', axes: [axis('Y1', '0'), axis('Y2', '5000')] },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(duplicate.grids).toEqual([\r\n      { direction: 'Y', groupName: 'Y', axes: [{ label: 'Y1' }, { label: 'Y2' }], spansMm: [5000] },\r\n    ])\r\n    expect(duplicate.issues).toEqual(['?싥굤??퐤營?뇥筽?])\r\n\r\n    const insufficient = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        axisGroups: [\r\n          { groupName: 'X', angle: '270', axes: [axis('X1', '0')] },\r\n          { groupName: 'Y', angle: '0', axes: [axis('Y1', '0'), axis('Y2', '5000')] },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(insufficient.grids).toEqual([\r\n      { direction: 'Y', groupName: 'Y', axes: [{ label: 'Y1' }, { label: 'Y2' }], spansMm: [5000] },\r\n    ])\r\n    expect(insufficient.issues).toEqual(['?싥굤??쑋濾쒎눣'])\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  it('reports node mismatches without discarding the grid and includes the group origin', () => {\r\n    const mismatch = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        axisGroups: [\r\n          {\r\n            groupName: 'X',\r\n            angle: '270',\r\n            originX: '100',\r\n            axes: [axis('X1', '0', ['x1']), axis('X2', '6000', ['x2'])],\r\n          },\r\n          {\r\n            groupName: 'Y',\r\n            angle: '0',\r\n            originY: '200',\r\n            axes: [axis('Y1', '0', ['y1']), axis('Y2', '5000', ['y2'])],\r\n          },\r\n        ],\r\n        nodes: [\r\n          { id: 'x1', x: '100', y: '0' },\r\n          { id: 'x2', x: '6500', y: '0' },\r\n          { id: 'y1', x: '0', y: '200' },\r\n          { id: 'y2', x: '0', y: '5000' },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(mismatch.grids).toHaveLength(2)\r\n    expect(mismatch.issues).toEqual(['?싥굤??퐤營?겏影?밤겗訝띴???])\r\n\r\n    const match = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        axisGroups: [\r\n          {\r\n            groupName: 'X',\r\n            angle: '270',\r\n            originX: '100',\r\n            axes: [axis('X1', '0', ['x1']), axis('X2', '6000', ['x2'])],\r\n          },\r\n          {\r\n            groupName: 'Y',\r\n            angle: '0',\r\n            originY: '200',\r\n            axes: [axis('Y1', '0', ['y1']), axis('Y2', '5000', ['y2'])],\r\n          },\r\n        ],\r\n        nodes: [\r\n          { id: 'x1', x: '100', y: '0' },\r\n          { id: 'x2', x: '6100', y: '0' },\r\n          { id: 'y1', x: '0', y: '200' },\r\n          { id: 'y2', x: '0', y: '5200' },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(match.issues).not.toContain('?싥굤??퐤營?겏影?밤겗訝띴???)\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  it('rejects an incomplete story stack as a whole and derives adjacent heights', () => {\r\n    const candidate = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        stories: [\r\n          { name: '1FL', height: '200', kind: 'GENERAL' },\r\n          { name: '2FL', height: '4700', kind: 'GENERAL' },\r\n          { name: 'RFL', height: '8700', kind: 'ROOF' },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(candidate.stories).toEqual([\r\n      { name: '1FL', heightMm: 4500 },\r\n      { name: '2FL', heightMm: 4000 },\r\n    ])\r\n\r\n    const basement = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        stories: [\r\n          { name: 'B1F', height: '-3000', kind: 'BASEMENT' },\r\n          { name: '1FL', height: '0', kind: 'GENERAL' },\r\n          { name: 'RFL', height: '4000', kind: 'ROOF' },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(basement.stories).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(basement.issues).toEqual(['?겻툔?с깧?ユ쑋野얍퓶'])\r\n\r\n    const unsupportedKind = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        stories: [\r\n          { name: '1FL', height: '0', kind: 'GENERAL' },\r\n          { name: 'ISO', height: '4000', kind: 'ISOLATION' },\r\n          { name: 'RFL', height: '8000', kind: 'ROOF' },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(unsupportedKind.stories).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(unsupportedKind.issues).toEqual(['野얍퓶鸚뽧겗?롧Ŧ??])\r\n\r\n    const twoUnsupportedKinds = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        stories: [\r\n          { name: 'B1F', height: '-3000', kind: 'BASEMENT' },\r\n          { name: 'ISO', height: '0', kind: 'ISOLATION' },\r\n          { name: 'RFL', height: '4000', kind: 'ROOF' },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(twoUnsupportedKinds.stories).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(twoUnsupportedKinds.issues).toEqual([\r\n      '?겻툔?с깧?ユ쑋野얍퓶',\r\n      '野얍퓶鸚뽧겗?롧Ŧ??,\r\n    ])\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  it('accepts ROOF and PENTHOUSE, rejects invalid heights/names/duplicates/short stacks', () => {\r\n    expect(\r\n      toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n        document({\r\n          stories: [\r\n            { name: '1FL', height: '0', kind: 'GENERAL' },\r\n            { name: 'PH', height: '4000', kind: 'PENTHOUSE' },\r\n            { name: 'RFL', height: '8000', kind: 'ROOF' },\r\n          ],\r\n        }),\r\n      ).issues,\r\n    ).toEqual([])\r\n\r\n    const invalidHeight = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        stories: [\r\n          { name: '1FL', height: undefined, kind: 'GENERAL' },\r\n          { name: 'RFL', height: '4000', kind: 'ROOF' },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(invalidHeight.stories).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(invalidHeight.issues).toEqual(['?롢꺃?쇻꺂鰲ｉ뇠訝띹꺗'])\r\n    expect(JSON.stringify(invalidHeight)).not.toContain('heightMm\":0')\r\n\r\n    const duplicate = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        stories: [\r\n          { name: '1FL', height: '0', kind: 'GENERAL' },\r\n          { name: '2FL', height: '4000', kind: 'GENERAL' },\r\n          { name: 'RFL', height: '4000', kind: 'ROOF' },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(duplicate.stories).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(duplicate.issues).toEqual(['?롢꺃?쇻꺂?띹쨭'])\r\n\r\n    const insufficient = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({ stories: [{ name: '1FL', height: '0', kind: 'GENERAL' }] }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(insufficient.stories).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(insufficient.issues).toEqual(['?롣툖擁?])\r\n\r\n    const empty = toSkeletonCandidate(document({ stories: [] }))\r\n    expect(empty.stories).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(empty.issues).toEqual(['?롣툖擁?])\r\n\r\n    const negative = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        stories: [\r\n          { name: 'B1F', height: '-3000', kind: 'GENERAL' },\r\n          { name: '1FL', height: '0', kind: 'GENERAL' },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(negative.stories).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(negative.issues).toEqual(['?겻툔?с깧?ユ쑋野얍퓶'])\r\n\r\n    const missingName = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        stories: [\r\n          { name: undefined, height: '0', kind: 'GENERAL' },\r\n          { name: 'RFL', height: '4000', kind: 'ROOF' },\r\n        ],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(missingName.stories).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(missingName.issues).toEqual(['?롢꺃?쇻꺂鰲ｉ뇠訝띹꺗'])\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  it('copies document failures and unsupported elements without producing candidates', () => {\r\n    const failed = toSkeletonCandidate(\r\n      document({\r\n        issues: ['野얍퓶鸚뽧깘?쇈궦?㎯꺍'],\r\n        unsupportedAxisKinds: [{ name: 'StbArcAxes', count: 2 }],\r\n        unreadElements: [{ name: 'StbColumn', count: 3 }],\r\n      }),\r\n    )\r\n    expect(failed.grids).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(failed.stories).toEqual([])\r\n    expect(failed.issues).toEqual(['野얍퓶鸚뽧깘?쇈궦?㎯꺍'])\r\n    expect(failed.unsupported).toEqual([\r\n      { name: 'StbArcAxes', count: 2 },\r\n      { name: 'StbColumn', count: 3 },\r\n    ])\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  it('returns a JSON-only candidate', () => {\r\n    const candidate = toSkeletonCandidate(document({ projectName: 'demo' }))\r\n    expect(JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(candidate))).toEqual(candidate)\r\n  })\r\n})\r\n\r\n===== src/components/stb/StbImport.tsx =====\r\n'use client'\n\nimport { useRef, useState, type ChangeEvent } from 'react'\n\nimport { decodeStbBytes } from '@/lib/import/stb/decode'\nimport { parseStbDocument } from '@/lib/import/stb/document'\nimport { toSkeletonCandidate } from '@/lib/import/stb/candidates'\nimport { applyStbGrid, applyStbStories } from '@/lib/import/stb/apply'\nimport type { StbGridCandidate, StbSkeletonCandidate } from '@/lib/import/stb/types'\nimport { t } from '@/lib/i18n'\nimport { useAppStore } from '@/lib/store'\n\nimport styles from './StbImport.module.css'\n\ninterface StbImportProps {\n  /** ?뚯뒪?몄뿉???뚯씪 ?댁꽍??嫄대꼫?곌퀬 ?꾨낫瑜?吏곸젒 ?ｋ뒗 而댄룷?뚰듃 ?뚯뒪?몄슜 寃쎄퀎. */\n  initialCandidate?: StbSkeletonCandidate\n}\n\ntype GridApplyResult = ReturnType<typeof applyStbGrid>\ntype StoriesApplyResult = ReturnType<typeof applyStbStories>\n\nfunction GridCandidate({\n  candidate,\n  locale,\n}: {\n  candidate: StbGridCandidate\n  locale: 'ja' | 'ko'\n}) {\n  return (\n    <div className={styles.group} data-testid={`stb-import-grid-${candidate.direction}`}>\n      <h4 className={styles.groupTitle}>\n        {t(\n          locale,\n          candidate.direction === 'X' ? 'stbImport.gridX' : 'stbImport.gridY',\n        )}\n      </h4>\n      <p className={styles.axes}>\n        {candidate.axes.map((axis, index) => (\n          <span key={`${axis.label}-${index}`}>\n            <span className={styles.axis}>{axis.label}</span>\n            {index < candidate.spansMm.length ? (\n              <span className={styles.span}>\n                {` ??${candidate.spansMm[index]} ??`}\n              </span>\n            ) : null}\n          </span>\n        ))}\n      </p>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction ApplyResult({\n  result,\n  locale,\n  successKey,\n  count,\n  testId,\n}: {\n  result: GridApplyResult | StoriesApplyResult | null\n  locale: 'ja' | 'ko'\n  successKey: 'stbImport.appliedGrid' | 'stbImport.appliedStories'\n  count: number\n  testId: string\n}) {\n  if (!result) return null\n\n  return (\n    <p className={styles.result} data-testid={testId}>\n      {result.refusal\n        ? t(locale, `stbImport.refusal.${result.refusal}`)\n        : `${t(locale, successKey)}: ${count}`}\n    </p>\n  )\n}\n\nexport function StbImport({ initialCandidate }: StbImportProps) {\n  const locale = useAppStore(({ locale }) => locale)\n  const updateProject = useAppStore(({ updateProject }) => updateProject)\n  const inputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null)\n  const [candidate, setCandidate] = useState<StbSkeletonCandidate | null>(\n    initialCandidate ?? null,\n  )\n  const [open, setOpen] = useState(initialCandidate !== undefined)\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false)\n  const [failed, setFailed] = useState(false)\n  const [gridResult, setGridResult] = useState<GridApplyResult | null>(null)\n  const [storiesResult, setStoriesResult] = useState<StoriesApplyResult | null>(\n    null,\n  )\n  const [discardGridMembers, setDiscardGridMembers] = useState(false)\n  const [discardStoryMembers, setDiscardStoryMembers] = useState(false)\n  const requestRef = useRef(0)\n\n  const selectFile = async (event: ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {\n    const input = event.currentTarget\n    const file = input.files?.[0]\n    if (!file) return\n\n    const requestId = ++requestRef.current\n    setOpen(true)\n    setLoading(true)\n    setFailed(false)\n    setCandidate(null)\n    setGridResult(null)\n    setStoriesResult(null)\n    setDiscardGridMembers(false)\n    setDiscardStoryMembers(false)\n\n    try {\n      const decoded = decodeStbBytes(await file.arrayBuffer())\n      if (requestRef.current !== requestId) return\n\n      if (!decoded.ok) {\n        setCandidate({\n          version: '??,\n          grids: [],\n          stories: [],\n          unsupported: [],\n          issues: [decoded.issue],\n        })\n      } else {\n        const document = parseStbDocument(decoded.text, decoded.encoding)\n        setCandidate(toSkeletonCandidate(document))\n      }\n    } catch {\n      if (requestRef.current !== requestId) return\n      setCandidate(null)\n      setFailed(true)\n    } finally {\n      if (requestRef.current === requestId) setLoading(false)\n      input.value = ''\n    }\n  }\n\n  const applyGrid = () => {\n    if (!candidate) return\n\n    let next: GridApplyResult | undefined\n    updateProject((project) => {\n      next = applyStbGrid(project, candidate, {\n        discardMembers: discardGridMembers,\n      })\n      return next.project\n    })\n    if (next) setGridResult(next)\n  }\n\n  const applyStories = () => {\n    if (!candidate) return\n\n    let next: StoriesApplyResult | undefined\n    updateProject((project) => {\n      next = applyStbStories(project, candidate, {\n        discardMembers: discardStoryMembers,\n      })\n      return next.project\n    })\n    if (next) setStoriesResult(next)\n  }\n\n  const hasGridCandidate =\n    candidate?.grids.filter(({ direction }) => direction === 'X').length === 1 &&\n    candidate.grids.filter(({ direction }) => direction === 'Y').length === 1\n  const hasStoryCandidate = candidate !== null && candidate.stories.length > 0\n\n  return (\n    <div className={styles.control}>\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        className={styles.openButton}\n        onClick={() => {\n          if (candidate) setOpen(true)\n          else inputRef.current?.click()\n        }}\n      >\n        {t(locale, 'stbImport.open')}\n      </button>\n      <input\n        ref={inputRef}\n        className={styles.fileInput}\n        data-testid=\"stb-import-file\"\n        type=\"file\"\n        accept=\".stb\"\n        aria-label={t(locale, 'stbImport.file')}\n        onChange={(event) => void selectFile(event)}\n      />\n\n      {open ? (\n        <section\n          className={styles.panel}\n          role=\"dialog\"\n          aria-modal=\"false\"\n          aria-labelledby=\"stb-import-title\"\n        >\n          <header className={styles.panelHeader}>\n            <h3 id=\"stb-import-title\" data-testid=\"stb-import-title\">\n              {t(locale, 'stbImport.title')}\n            </h3>\n            <div className={styles.panelActions}>\n              <button\n                type=\"button\"\n                className={styles.chooseButton}\n                onClick={() => inputRef.current?.click()}\n              >\n                {t(locale, 'stbImport.chooseAnother')}\n              </button>\n              <button\n                type=\"button\"\n                className={styles.closeButton}\n                onClick={() => setOpen(false)}\n              >\n                {t(locale, 'stbImport.close')}\n              </button>\n            </div>\n          </header>\n\n          <div className={styles.panelBody}>\n            {loading ? (\n              <p role=\"status\">{t(locale, 'stbImport.loading')}</p>\n            ) : failed ? (\n              <p role=\"alert\">{t(locale, 'stbImport.error')}</p>\n            ) : candidate ? (\n              <>\n                <div className={styles.metadata}>\n                  <span data-testid=\"stb-import-version\">\n                    {`${t(locale, 'stbImport.version')}: ${candidate.version}`}\n                  </span>\n                  {candidate.projectName !== undefined ? (\n                    <span data-testid=\"stb-import-project-name\">\n                      {`${t(locale, 'stbImport.projectName')}: ${candidate.projectName}`}\n                    </span>\n                  ) : null}\n                </div>\n\n                {candidate.issues.length > 0 ? (\n                  <section className={styles.group} data-testid=\"stb-import-issues\">\n                    <h4 className={styles.groupTitle}>\n                      {t(locale, 'stbImport.issues')}\n                    </h4>\n                    <ul className={styles.issues}>\n                      {[...new Set(candidate.issues)].map((issue) => (\n                        <li key={issue}>{t(locale, `stbImport.issue.${issue}`)}</li>\n                      ))}\n                    </ul>\n                  </section>\n                ) : null}\n\n                <section className={styles.group}>\n                  <h4 className={styles.groupTitle}>\n                    {t(locale, 'stbImport.grids')}\n                  </h4>\n                  {candidate.grids.map((grid, index) => (\n                    <GridCandidate\n                      key={`${grid.direction}-${index}`}\n                      candidate={grid}\n                      locale={locale}\n                    />\n                  ))}\n                  {hasGridCandidate ? (\n                    <button\n                      type=\"button\"\n                      className={styles.applyButton}\n                      data-testid=\"stb-import-apply-grid\"\n                      onClick={applyGrid}\n                    >\n                      {t(locale, 'stbImport.applyGrid')}\n                    </button>\n                  ) : null}\n                  {gridResult?.refusal === '?ⓩ쓲?귙굤?싥굤??쉰?쎽툖?? ? (\n                    <label className={styles.discardOption}>\n                      <input\n                        type=\"checkbox\"\n                        data-testid=\"stb-import-discard-grid\"\n                        checked={discardGridMembers}\n                        onChange={(event) =>\n                          setDiscardGridMembers(event.target.checked)\n                        }\n                      />\n                      {t(locale, 'stbImport.discardMembersGrid')}\n                    </label>\n                  ) : null}\n                  <ApplyResult\n                    result={gridResult}\n                    locale={locale}\n                    successKey=\"stbImport.appliedGrid\"\n                    count={candidate.grids.length}\n                    testId=\"stb-import-grid-result\"\n                  />\n                </section>\n\n                <section className={styles.group} data-testid=\"stb-import-stories\">\n                  <h4 className={styles.groupTitle}>\n                    {t(locale, 'stbImport.stories')}\n                  </h4>\n                  {candidate.stories.length > 0 ? (\n                    <ul className={styles.storyList}>\n                      {candidate.stories.map((story, index) => (\n                        <li key={`${story.name}-${index}`}>\n                          <span className={styles.axis}>{story.name}</span>\n                          <span className={styles.span}>\n                            {` ??${story.heightMm} ${t(locale, 'stbImport.height')} ??`}\n                          </span>\n                        </li>\n                      ))}\n                    </ul>\n                  ) : (\n                    <p className={styles.muted}>{t(locale, 'stbImport.none')}</p>\n                  )}\n                  {hasStoryCandidate ? (\n                    <button\n                      type=\"button\"\n                      className={styles.applyButton}\n                      data-testid=\"stb-import-apply-stories\"\n                      onClick={applyStories}\n                    >\n                      {t(locale, 'stbImport.applyStories')}\n                    </button>\n                  ) : null}\n                  {storiesResult?.refusal === '?ⓩ쓲?귙굤?롧쉰?쎽툖?? ? (\n                    <label className={styles.discardOption}>\n                      <input\n                        type=\"checkbox\"\n                        data-testid=\"stb-import-discard-stories\"\n                        checked={discardStoryMembers}\n                        onChange={(event) =>\n                          setDiscardStoryMembers(event.target.checked)\n                        }\n                      />\n                      {t(locale, 'stbImport.discardMembersStories')}\n                    </label>\n                  ) : null}\n                  <ApplyResult\n                    result={storiesResult}\n                    locale={locale}\n                    successKey=\"stbImport.appliedStories\"\n                    count={candidate.stories.length}\n                    testId=\"stb-import-stories-result\"\n                  />\n                </section>\n\n                <section className={styles.group} data-testid=\"stb-import-unsupported\">\n                  <h4 className={styles.groupTitle}>\n                    {`${t(locale, 'stbImport.unsupported')} (${candidate.unsupported.length})`}\n                  </h4>\n                  {candidate.unsupported.length > 0 ? (\n                    <ul className={styles.issues}>\n                      {candidate.unsupported.map(({ name, count }, index) => (\n                        <li key={`${name}-${index}`}>{`${name}: ${count}`}</li>\n                      ))}\n                    </ul>\n                  ) : (\n                    <p className={styles.muted}>{t(locale, 'stbImport.none')}</p>\n                  )}\n                </section>\n              </>\n            ) : null}\n          </div>\n        </section>\n      ) : null}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\r\n===== HEAD =====\r\nddf50fd chore(34-stbridge-apply): step 7 output\nace684e feat(34-stbridge-apply): step 7 — fix guard evasion and risk ledger\n9c68fac chore(34-stbridge-apply): step 7이 blocked로 지적한 사양 모순을 고친다\n===== STATUS =====\r\n M phases/34-stbridge-apply/index.json\n?? phases/34-stbridge-apply/step8-codex.stderr.log\n?? phases/34-stbridge-apply/step8-codex.stdout.log\n===== PHASE FILES =====\r\nindex.json\r\nstep0-codex.stderr.log\r\nstep0-codex.stdout.log\r\nstep0-invoke.json\r\nstep0-report.json\r\nstep0.md\r\nstep1-codex.stderr.log\r\nstep1-codex.stdout.log\r\nstep1-invoke.json\r\nstep1.md\r\nstep2-codex.stderr.log\r\nstep2-codex.stdout.log\r\nstep2-invoke.json\r\nstep2.md\r\nstep3-codex.stderr.log\r\nstep3-codex.stdout.log\r\nstep3-invoke.json\r\nstep3.md\r\nstep4-codex.stderr.log\r\nstep4-codex.stdout.log\r\nstep4-invoke.json\r\nstep4.md\r\nstep5-codex.stderr.log\r\nstep5-codex.stdout.log\r\nstep5-invoke.json\r\nstep5.md\r\nstep6-codex.stderr.log\r\nstep6-codex.stdout.log\r\nstep6-invoke.json\r\nstep6-report.json\r\nstep6.md\r\nstep7-codex.stderr.log\r\nstep7-codex.stdout.log\r\nstep7-invoke.json\r\nstep7-report.json\r\nstep7.md\r\nstep8-codex.stderr.log\r\nstep8-codex.stdout.log\r\nstep8.md\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
